main.content:
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈvɛst/|a=RP,GA,CA}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-invest.wav|a=London}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-invest.ogg|a=California}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈvest/|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛst|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|id=spend for benefit|:bor|frm:investir<ety:der<la:investio>>|la-med:investire<ety:der<la:investio>>}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|frm|investir}} or {{bor|en|la-med|investire}}, from {{der|en|la|investio||to clothe, cover}}, from {{m|la|in-||in, on}} + {{m|la|vestio||to clothe, dress}}, from {{m|la|vestis||clothing}}; see {{m|en|vest}}. The sense “to spend money etc.” probably via {{der|en|it|investire}}, of the same root.<ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref>

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# To spend money, [[time]], or [[energy]] on something, especially for some [[benefit]] or [[purpose]]; used with ''in''.
#: {{ux|en|We'd like to thank all the contributors who have '''invested''' countless hours into this event.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=4 November 2025|author=Thomas Kelly|title=Debunking “When Prophecy Fails”
|work=Journal of the History of the Behavioral Sciences|volume=62|issue=1|issn=1520-6696|doi=10.1002/jhbs.70043|page=1|passage=The authors predicted that when believers were deeply '''invested''' in a world view that had social support, believers would maintain their beliefs even when actual events disproved their worldview.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|author=NY Times DealBook Summit|date=Dec 3, 2025|title=MrBeast on Cracking the Attention Economy|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N9gSO66oC6U|speaker=w:Jimmy Donaldson|at=29:21|passage=We did not spend. We '''invested'''. [CEO Jeff Housenbold: He's learning!] I '''invest'''. Yes, I '''invested'''. I '''invested''' in a city for the contestants.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|dated}} To [[clothe]] or [[wrap]] (with garments).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1851|author=Herman Melville|title=Moby-Dick|passage=He was but shabbily apparelled in faded jacket and patched trowsers; a rag of a black handkerchief '''investing''' his neck.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|obsolete}} To [[put on]] (clothing).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1596|author=w:Edmund Spenser|title=w:The Faerie Queene|others=book 4, canto 5, verse 18|passage=Cannot find one this girdle to '''invest'''!}}
# To [[envelop]], [[wrap]], [[cover]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1667|author=w:John Milton|title=w:Paradise Lost|others=Book 1, ll. 207-8|passage=Night / '''Invests''' the Sea, and wished Morn delayes}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1875|author=Charles Lyell|title=The Principles of Geology|edition=12|page=39|volume=1|text=When the outer crust had cooled down sufficiently to allow the vapours to be condensed, they fell, and formed a universal ocean, covering the loftiest mountains, and '''investing''' the whole globe.}}
# To [[commit]] [[money]] or [[capital]] in the [[hope]] of [[financial]] [[gain]].
# To [[ceremonially]] [[install]] someone in some [[office]].
# To [[formally]] give (someone) some [[power]] or [[authority]].
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=ii|page=22|passage=Madam, whatſoeuer you eſteeme<br>Of this ſucceſſe, and loſſe vnualued,<br>Both may '''inueſt''' you Empreſſe of the Eaſt: {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=c. 1603–06|author=w:William Shakespeare|title=w:King Lear|section=act 1, scene 1|passage=I do '''invest''' you jointly with my power.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1965|author=Parliament of Malaysia|title=Syariah Courts (Criminal Jurisdiction) Act 1965 (1988 R. Ed.)|chapter=Section 1|url=https://lom.agc.gov.my/ilims/upload/portal/akta/outputaktap/2263446_BI/Act%20355%20Revised.pdf|page=5|text=The Syariah Courts duly constituted under any law in a State and '''invested''' with jurisdiction over persons professing the religion of Islam {{...}} are hereby conferred jurisdiction in respect of offences against precepts of the religion of Islam by persons professing that religion which may be prescribed under any written law {{...}}}}
# To [[formally]] give (power or authority).
#: {{syn|en|confer}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=a. 1626|author=w:Francis Bacon|title=An Advertisement Touching a Holy War|passage=For he saith, if there can be found such an inequality between man and man, as there is between man and beast, or between soul and body, it '''investeth''' a right of government: which seemeth rather an impossible case than an untrue sentence.}}
# To [[surround]], [[accompany]], or [[attend]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1850|author=w:Nathaniel Hawthorne|title=w:The Scarlet Letter|passage=The scene was not without a mixture of awe such as must always '''invest''' the spectacle of the guilt and shame in a fellow-creature, before society shall have grown corrupt enough to smile, instead of shuddering, at it.}}
#* {{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|chapter=35|page=171|passage=For the most part, in this tropic whaling life, a sublime uneventfulness '''invests''' you; you hear no news; read no gazettes; extras with startling accounts of commonplaces never delude you into unnecessary excitements; you hear of no domestic afflictions; bankrupt securities; fall of stocks; are never troubled with the thought of what you shall have for dinner—for all your meals for three years and more are snugly stowed in casks, and your bill of fare is immutable.}}
# To lay [[siege]] to.
#: {{ux|en|to '''invest''' a town}}
#* {{RQ:Maturin Melmoth|IV||216|When she related that a band of fanatics, after robbing a church of all its silver-plate, and burning the adjacent vicarage, drunk with their success, had '''invested''' the Castle, and cried aloud for ‘''the man''’ to be brought unto them, that he might be hewed to pieces before the Lord in Gilgal—[…]her young hearers felt a deep stirring of the heart,—a proud yet mellowed elation that never yet was felt by the reader of a written history, though its pages were as legitimate as any sanctioned by the royal licenser at Madrid.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To make [[investments]].
# {{lb|en|metallurgy}} To prepare for [[lost wax]] casting by creating an investment mold (a mixture of a silica sand and plaster).
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To cause to be [[involve]]d in; to cause to form strong attachments to.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Michael D. Garval| title=A Dream of Stone| pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=jadTA5yudTcC&pg=PA214| isbn=9780874138627| page=214| publisher=University of Delaware Press| passage=From early on in his career, Zola's work as a critic revealed just how heavily he was '''invested''' in the literary “dream of stone.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Sarah Varland|title=Tundra Threat: Faith in the Face of Crime| pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=H210AwAAQBAJ&pg=PA107| isbn=9781460341278| page=107| publisher=Harlequin| passage=She knew from watching him grow up that he didn't let that many people too close to him, but once he did, he was '''invested''' in that relationship.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|author=James Graham|title=Tory Boyz| pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=HrfoBgAAQBAJ&pg=PT11| isbn=9781472587824| page=11| publisher=Bloomsbury Publishing| passage=We decided that it was because he trusted the core beliefs of the Conservative Party, and he was '''invested''' in their vision of change in the NorthWest of England where he comes from.}}
# {{lb|en|Spanish politics}} To [[inaugurate]] the {{w|Prime Minister of Spain}} after a successful parliamentary vote.
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2023-07-24|accessdate=2023-08-06|author=Carlos Cué|title=In Spain, the left's resistance thwarts a PP-Vox majority and leaves all possibilities open|work=w:El País|url=https://english.elpais.com/spain/2023-07-23/in-spain-the-lefts-resistance-thwarts-a-pp-vox-majority-and-leaves-all-possibilities-open.html|text=The outcome also makes it very difficult for Feijóo to become the next PM, because he does not have the support to be '''invested''' as such, unless there are changes in the initial positions of key players such as the Basque Nationalist Party (PNV).|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261005173852/https://english.elpais.com/spain/2023-07-23/in-spain-the-lefts-resistance-thwarts-a-pp-vox-majority-and-leaves-all-possibilities-open.html|archivedate=5 October 2026}}

