===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|kene||[[bold#Adjective|bold]], [[brave#Adjective|brave]], [[sharp#Adjective|sharp]]}}, from {{inh|en|ang|cēne||keen, [[fierce]], bold, brave, [[warlike]], [[powerful]]; [[learned#Adjective|learned]], [[clever]], [[wise#Adjective|wise]]}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*kōniz||[[knowledgeable]], [[skilful]], [[experienced]], [[clever]], [[capable]]}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ǵneh₃-||to [[know]]}}.

Cognate with {{cog|da|køn||[[handsome]], [[pretty]]}}, {{cog|nl|kien||[[smart#Adjective|smart]], wise, [[able#Adjective|able]]}}, {{m|nl|koen||[[daring#Adjective|daring]], [[valiant]], [[doughty]], [[courageous]]}}, {{cog|de|kühn||bold, daring, [[audacious]], [[hardy]], valiant, [[venturesome]]}}, {{cog|is|kænn||wise, crafty, clever, able}}, {{cog|fo|kønur||expert (in, on), experienced, skilful, able, capable}}, {{cog|sco|keen||[[lively]], [[brisk]]; [[avaricious]]}}. Related to {{cog|ang|cunnan||to know how to, [[be able to]]}}. More at {{m|en|cunning}}, {{m|en|can}}.

