===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|kag}}, from {{der|en|non|kaggi|t=keg}}, likely a diminutive of {{der|en|gem-pro|*kagô|t=bush, branch, stalk, stump}}. Cognate with {{cog|is|kaggi|t=keg; cask}}, {{cog|no|kagg|t=keg}}, {{cog|sv|kagge|t=keg}}, {{cog|nds|kag|t=vessel; craft}}, {{cog|nl|kaag|t=vessel; craft}}. Compare also {{cog|en|cag}} and {{m|en|chag}}.

The modern form ''keg'' with {{IPAchar|/ɛ/}} is due to a dialectal raising of {{IPAchar|/a/}}/{{IPAchar|/æ/}} to {{IPAchar|/ɛ/}} before velars (cf. {{m|en|fleg}}); the expected form is preserved in dialectal {{IPAchar|/kæɡ/}}, while {{IPAchar|/keɪɡ/}} reflects further raising that occurred in some dialects.

