|passage=Having done what was required to gain admittance to the "'''kitchen'''," as the public rooms are termed, as well as to the more exclusive "Salle Privée" {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1953|author=Ian Fleming|title=Casino Royale|passage=But on this June evening when Bond walked through the ''''kitchen'''' into the salle privée, it was with a sensation of confidence and cheerful anticipation that he changed a million francs into plaques of fifty mille and took a seat {{...}}}}
