===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*yewg-}}
The noun is from {{inh|en|enm|joynt}} (attested since the late 13th century), from {{der|en|fro|joint|t=joint of the body}} (attested since the 12th century). The adjective (attested since the 15th century) is from {{cog|fro|jointiz}}. Both Old French words are from {{der|en|la|iūnctus}}, the past participle of {{m|la|iungō}}. See also {{m|en|join}}, {{m|en|jugular}}, {{m|en|junction}}. Displaced {{noncog|ang|fōg}} and partially displaced {{noncog|en|lith}}.

The meaning of "building, establishment", especially in connection with shady activities, appeared in Anglo-Irish by 1821 and entered general American English slang by 1877, especially in the sense of "opium den". The sense "marijuana cigarette" is attested since 1935. The development to meaning "any thing" also happened to the Scots and Memphian form {{m|en|junt}} and the Mid-Atlantic/Philadelphian form {{m|en|jawn}}.

