===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The state or characteristic of being [[just]] or [[fair]].
#: {{ux|en|the '''justice''' of a description}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Macbeth|I|vii|passage=This even-handed '''justice''' / Commends the ingredients of our poisoned chalice / To our own lips.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=David L. Lieber; Jules Harlow|title=Etz Hayim: Torah and Commentary|page=8|text=God recognized the '''justice''' of the moon's plea and compensated for its diminution by promising that only the moon would be seen both day and night.}}
# The ideal of [[fairness]], [[impartiality]], etc., especially with regard to the [[punishment]] of [[wrongdoing]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Justice''' was served.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1978|last=Kołakowski|first=Leszek|authorlink=Leszek Kołakowski|title=w:Main Currents of Marxism|volume=II: The Golden Age|origlang=pl|original=Główne nurty marksizmu: rozwój|translator=P[aul] S[teven] Falla|origyear=1976|publisher=w:Clarendon Press|location=w:Oxford|isbn=9780198245698|oclc=961252281|page=145|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/maincurrentsofma00lesz/page/145|passage=The perfect society is not to be an embodiment of the idea of '''justice''', but one in which that idea has no meaning, since it is bound up with private property and the regulation of property relationships.}}
# [[judgment|Judgment]] and punishment of a party who has [[alleged]]ly [[wrong]]ed another.
#: {{ux|en|to demand '''justice'''}}
# The [[civil]] power dealing with [[law]].
#: {{ux|en|Ministry of '''Justice'''}}
#: {{ux|en|the '''justice''' system}}
# A title given to [[judge]]s of certain [[court]]s (usually [[supreme court]]s); [[capitalize]]d when placed before a name.
#: {{syn|en|q1=judge of a superior court|justiciar|justiciary|Thesaurus:judge}}
#: {{ux|en|Mr. '''Justice''' Krever presides over the appellate court}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-US|author=Gail Collins|title=Trump Is the Leading Man|work=The New York Times|date=2024-03-04|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/03/04/opinion/trump-mcconnell-biden.html|issn=0362-4331|author2=Bret Stephens|passage= Gee, I guess that’s up to the '''justices'''. Can’t imagine this court — which I find too conservative but not crazy — is going to issue a ruling that says a president can break any law in the land as an “official act” without consequence.}}
# [[correctness|Correctness]], [[conform]]ing to reality or rules.
#* {{RQ:Swift Gulliver|part=I|pages=106–107|pageref=106|passage=As to Perſons of Quality, they give Security to appropriate a certain Sum for each Child, ſuitable to their Condition; and theſe Funds are always managed with good Husbandry and the moſt exact '''Juſtice'''.}}

