## {{lb|en|group algebra}} A [[bijection]] ''f'' such that both ''f'' and its [[inverse function|inverse]] ''f''<sup>&nbsp;&minus;1</sup> are [[homomorphism]]s, that is, structure-preserving mappings. {{C|en|Functions}}
## {{lb|en|computer science}} a [[one-to-one]] [[correspondence]] between all the [[element]]s of two [[set]]s, e.g. the [[instance]]s of two [[class]]es, or the [[record]]s in two [[dataset]]s.
